# Reason service (Go)

Consume `github.pr.opened`. Fetch pull body and changed files (token + User-Agent). Do not classify from title alone.

Rules are an **ordered list** (after fetch): all `.md` → `docs`; all lockfiles → `dependency-bump`. Mixed trees go to the Model. Empty file list is not `docs`.

Loop: Summarize, then Classification. Parse dirty JSON (first `{...}`), normalize labels, retry, then `unknown`. Upsert Postgres on `event_id`. Labels: `security|feature|refactor|docs|dependency-bump|unknown`. `source` is `rule`, `model`, or `fallback`.

```go
// ❌ BAD
category := "docs" // from strings.Contains(title, "readme")

// ✅ GOOD — Rules on fetched file names only
if out, ok := matchRules(in); ok {
    return out
}
```

Ack after successful upsert. Postgres errors: do not ack. Enum, Rules, and parse stay as functions (extension seams).

Details: `.cursor/spec/architecture.md`, `.cursor/spec/decisions.md`.
